# Sample requests for the external API (/api/v1/todos).
# Start the app first: dotnet run --project src/BlazorWebApplication.Server --launch-profile https
# Visual Studio, Rider and VS Code (with the REST Client extension) can send these requests.
#
# The API needs an Entra ID access token (step 11). Get one and paste it below:
#   az account get-access-token --scope api://<client-id>/.default --query accessToken -o tsv
# Reading needs the Reader or Api.Writer role; creating, changing and deleting needs Api.Writer.

@host = https://localhost:7029
@token = <paste-access-token-here>

### List all todos
GET {{host}}/api/v1/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Create a todo (the response contains its id)
# @name createTodo
POST {{host}}/api/v1/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Try the external API"
}

### Get the new todo (send "Create a todo" first)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/todos/{{createTodo.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Mark it as done
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/todos/{{createTodo.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Try the external API",
  "isDone": true
}

### Delete it
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/todos/{{createTodo.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An empty title returns 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/v1/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": ""
}

### An unknown id returns 404 Not Found
GET {{host}}/api/v1/todos/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token you get 401 Unauthorized
GET {{host}}/api/v1/todos
